 ],
 "text": "Not every AI step needs a chatbot. OpenAI's new decision model picks between options in about 100 milliseconds. A chat model takes 1 to 3 seconds. Speak says its weight between steps fell from 1.4 seconds to 0.13. Most AI work isn't writing, it's choosing. Here's where that fits. 1. Routing. Which inbox, which team, and how sure it is. 2. Picking. Which reply, which tool, what happens next. 3. Flagging. Spam, urgent, or fine in a blink. When it's not sure, a person decides. The chat model still writes the reply. The decision model picks the lane. Want my AI starter pack? Comment AI and I'll send it to you free."
